<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yoweri Museveni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yoweri Museveni is a Ugandan politician and former rebel leader who has been President of Uganda since 1986. Born in Ankole, he fought against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idi-amin">Idi Amin</a> and then led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-resistance-army">National Resistance Army</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ugandan-bush-war">Ugandan Bush War</a>, which brought him to power. He restored the traditional kingdoms as cultural institutions in 1993, and constitutional changes removed term and age limits on his presidency.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yoweri-museveni.jpg" alt="Yoweri Museveni" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DFID - UK Department for International Development · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Museveni_July_2012_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
